= The Rise of ISIS

The Islamic State has seized Mosul and proclaims a caliphate. Pressure mounts for American military action in Iraq and Syria. Public opinion is weary after a decade of war.

- @isis_strikes: Back limited air strikes
- @isis_vote: Demand a congressional vote
- @isis_oppose: Oppose any new military action

@isis_strikes
on-arrival: moderate_strength += 2; intl_relation += 2; progressive_dissent += 5; military_loyalty += 0.02

We support targeted strikes and support for local partners. The left is uneasy.

@isis_vote
on-arrival: institutions += 1; progressive_strength += 1; moderate_dissent += 2; pro_democracy += 0.5

We insist Congress, not the president alone, authorize any war.

@isis_oppose
on-arrival: progressive_strength += 3; progressive_dissent -= 4; moderate_dissent += 5; intl_relation -= 2

We warn of another quagmire. The base cheers; hawks worry.
